1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:12,570
Asked for 3 s. Got 13 frames, 0.52 s.

2
00:00:12,570 --> 00:00:20,550
Where does a cut really start?

3
00:00:20,550 --> 00:00:27,350
Five things decide your cut.

4
00:00:27,350 --> 00:00:38,240
Each one is measured on a test clip.

5
00:00:38,240 --> 00:00:46,150
Reader 1: frame md5 against the source.

6
00:00:46,150 --> 00:00:56,330
Reader 2: ffprobe, or the number in the pixels.

7
00:00:56,330 --> 00:01:06,530
-ss 5 -to 10 -i: 5 s, 125 frames.

8
00:01:06,530 --> 00:01:12,190
Both after -i: the same.

9
00:01:12,190 --> 00:01:24,270
-ss 5 -i ... -to 10: 10 s, 250 frames.

10
00:01:24,270 --> 00:01:31,520
Source 5 s to 15 s.

11
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:42,830
-ss 5 -i ... -t 5: 5 s, source 5 to 10.

12
00:01:42,830 --> 00:01:48,490
So far: re-encoded. Next: -c copy.

13
00:01:48,490 --> 00:01:57,970
-ss before -i: 7.52 s, 75 frames.

14
00:01:57,970 --> 00:02:08,810
138 packets in the file. 63 are hidden.

15
00:02:08,810 --> 00:02:19,620
-ss after -i: starts at 10 s. 13 frames.

16
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:25,630
Re-encode: frame 188, 74 frames.

17
00:02:25,630 --> 00:02:35,290
-g 100 alone: 0, 3.2, 6.8.

18
00:02:35,290 --> 00:02:44,950
A maximum. Scene cuts add keyframes.

19
00:02:44,950 --> 00:02:56,270
+ -sc_threshold 0: 0, 4, 8.

20
00:02:56,270 --> 00:03:01,930
-force_key_frames 3.2,6.8: exact.

21
00:03:01,930 --> 00:03:11,520
-sseof -3, re-encode: 90 frames.

22
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:26,870
-c copy, -g 100: 100 frames, 3.333 s.

23
00:03:26,870 --> 00:03:36,810
10 s picture, 12 s sound: 1 s of picture.

24
00:03:36,810 --> 00:03:44,760
-sseof -30 on 10 s: all 300 frames.

25
00:03:44,760 --> 00:04:02,250
-shortest -c copy: 73 of 125 frames.

26
00:04:02,250 --> 00:04:09,750
Re-encode: 75 frames.

27
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:18,500
-t 3 -c copy: 77 frames, 3.08 s.

28
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:25,060
Copy: 73 or 77. Re-encode: 75.

29
00:04:25,060 --> 00:04:39,480
-ss 7.5 -i ... -t 3: 90 frames, 225 to 314.

30
00:04:39,480 --> 00:04:48,650
Control, -c copy after -i: 15 frames.

31
00:04:48,650 --> 00:04:56,450
Plain copy: 165 packets, 75 hidden.

32
00:04:56,450 --> 00:05:06,860
Keyframes at the cut: 90 frames, 90 packets.

33
00:05:06,860 --> 00:05:14,380
Exact: -ss, -i, -t, re-encode.

34
00:05:14,380 --> 00:05:26,400
Instant: keyframes at the cut, then -c copy.

35
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:33,530
Measured on ffmpeg 6.1.1, synthetic clips.

36
00:05:33,530 --> 00:05:41,840
Not tested: real footage, players, other encoders.
